1
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:42,440
[She's Wild Fire]

2
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:47,820
[Episode 11: Just Business, No Feelings]

3
00:00:57,830 --> 00:01:00,070
[Restructuring Meeting of First Garment Factory]

4
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:01,280
Xie Nanfeng?

5
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,420
Why is she here?

6
00:01:04,519 --> 00:01:06,650
I have three things to announce today.

7
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:07,600
First,

8
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,080
we are about to launch

9
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,160
our very first core product:

10
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,520
wireless bras.

11
00:01:13,720 --> 00:01:15,280
How can it have shape without underwire?

12
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,340
Who would buy that?

13
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:20,640
Why must women, in our pursuit of beauty,

14
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:22,200
endure physical constraints

15
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:23,720
and sacrifice our health?

16
00:01:24,039 --> 00:01:26,300
This is the paradox we're about to break.

17
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,240
We want to create clothing

18
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,330
that makes the body feel truly free,

19
00:01:30,350 --> 00:01:34,150
making women feel confident
and comfortable.

20
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,200
The second thing:

21
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:38,960
effective immediately,

22
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:41,420
Chang Yongbin is relieved
of all his duties.

23
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,080
In my company,

24
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:45,920
self-serving parasites are not allowed.

25
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:47,360
What should we do?

26
00:01:47,979 --> 00:01:48,500
Get out.

27
00:01:48,530 --> 00:01:49,530
The third thing:

28
00:01:49,759 --> 00:01:52,160
we are going to build

29
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,800
a clothing brand
that truly belongs to women.

30
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,400
Blooming Path.

31
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:00,360
Our goal isn't just the domestic market,

32
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:03,040
but the whole world.

33
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:25,280
Looks like we're naturally in sync.

34
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:27,240
We never even need to rehearse our acts.

35
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:27,680
Yeah.

36
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:28,800
Not bad.

37
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:33,040
Are you free tonight?

38
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:35,520
I booked a table at that old restaurant.

39
00:02:41,680 --> 00:02:42,440
Nanfeng!

40
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:47,880
Tim!

41
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,440
Why are you back in China?

42
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,450
Look what I brought you.

43
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,240
Rye bread
from that classic Manhattan bakery.

44
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,800
Specially vacuum-sealed.

45
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:08,960
The one we always went to?

46
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,400
Yeah.

47
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:11,600
Thanks, Tim.

48
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,130
Where's my baby boy?

49
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,480
And you are?

50
00:03:27,079 --> 00:03:27,600
Hello,

51
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:29,070
I'm Zhang Guodong.

52
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:30,430
You can also call me Tim.

53
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,160
I'm Nanfeng's...

54
00:03:31,160 --> 00:03:33,400
He's my friend from college.

55
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,520
Oh, a college friend.

56
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,120
I'm Chu Chunsheng.

57
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:47,320
I'm Nanfeng's...

58
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,000
He's my partner.

59
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,380
I thought I was your only partner.

60
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,120
But congratulations,

61
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:02,840
Nanfeng.

62
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,520
During this trip in China,

63
00:04:03,520 --> 00:04:04,760
I can clearly feel

64
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,520
minds here have opened up a lot,

65
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,040
especially for women.

66
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,320
Bringing those American concepts back here

67
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:12,240
was definitely the right call.

68
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,080
Open-mindedness grew

69
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,610
right out of this very land.

70
00:04:16,640 --> 00:04:17,959
Nobody brought it back.

71
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:19,480
People dare to dream and act

72
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:22,210
because of the vitality
and opportunities here.

73
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,400
Open and radical women

74
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:30,360
have always existed since ancient times.

75
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,830
It's not that they lack thoughts,

76
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:33,490
or fear breaking boundaries.

77
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,600
All they lacked was a stage

78
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,520
to release themselves

79
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,520
and show who they are.

80
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,520
Well said.

81
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:47,440
Tell you what,

82
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:48,770
dinner is on me tonight.

83
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,240
Let's have a real celebration.

84
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:51,970
Sounds good?

85
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,200
No need to celebrate.

86
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,370
I already booked a restaurant.

87
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:01,360
Let's go.

88
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:07,840
Tim,

89
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,600
you came back
for the New York business, right?

90
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,400
Why don't we discuss that first?

91
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:14,600
Mr. Chu,

92
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:17,300
how about we postpone
our celebration a bit?

93
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,040
Let's go, Tim.

94
00:05:24,880 --> 00:05:25,680
I'm going too.

95
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,600
Thanks, Tim.

96
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:44,570
Congrats, Nanfeng.

97
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,400
Back when you started your brand in the US

98
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,800
and came to me for funding,

99
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,640
I told you

100
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:52,380
you'd definitely achieve something great.

101
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:54,920
That's all thanks to you, Tim.

102
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,980
By the way, Tim,

103
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:00,880
you came back so suddenly,

104
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,810
did something happen
with our New York partnership?

105
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:04,800
Don't worry.

106
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,120
The partnership is going smoothly.

107
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,720
Just a few important documents
for you to sign.

108
00:06:10,440 --> 00:06:13,100
Of course, personal matters
are important too.

109
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,240
After all,

110
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:17,000
I didn't want to miss your big moment.

111
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:20,070
Tim,

112
00:06:20,090 --> 00:06:22,690
you still love joking around
just like before.

113
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,200
I'm serious.

114
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,490
When do you plan
on coming back to New York with me?

115
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:28,640
No!

116
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,130
You can't leave.

117
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,720
Chu Chunsheng?

118
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,000
Mr. Chu.

119
00:06:38,760 --> 00:06:39,720
Tim, let's go.

120
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,720
Why are you here?

121
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:39,810
Waiting for you.

122
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:42,580
Just like every single day

123
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,930
for the past five years.

124
00:07:49,159 --> 00:07:49,680
You're drunk.

125
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:50,640
Go home and rest.

126
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:58,790
♪ Before the raindrops fall,
blurring the view ♪

127
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,810
If you want to ask about Nannan,

128
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,320
I can...

129
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:01,320
I don't care who Nannan's father is.

130
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:05,810
♪ Memories replay like a silent film ♪

131
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,180
All I care about is who has been

132
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:08,320
by your side these past five years.

133
00:08:06,930 --> 00:08:13,660
♪ The warmth of your fingertips
has long faded in the wind ♪

134
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,320
It's over.

135
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:14,680
You mean you and him,

136
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:16,660
♪ The moment you turned away ♪

137
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,720
or you and me?

138
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,680
What's between him and me

139
00:08:17,710 --> 00:08:22,660
♪ Silence becomes so heavy ♪

140
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,480
is none of your business.

141
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,920
As for you and me,

142
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:31,410
♪ Why meet if we are destined to part ♪

143
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,720
we are partners.

144
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,820
We only talk business.

145
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:37,490
♪ Tears drown my breath ♪

146
00:08:38,169 --> 00:08:44,900
♪ The sound of a broken heart
in this merciless night ♪

147
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,520
I always thought

148
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:43,880
the longest-lasting relationship

149
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,240
was a business partnership.

150
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:51,870
♪ Only memories remain ♪

151
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,580
Until you didn't want me anymore.

152
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:55,120
I crossed the line.

153
00:08:54,410 --> 00:08:58,980
♪ I still want to cherish it ♪

154
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,600
From now on, I will fulfill

155
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,880
my duties as a partner.

156
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:05,530
♪ Please don't leave ♪

157
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,890
Why did you bring back this rotten mud?

158
00:09:17,770 --> 00:09:24,710
♪ Can time turn back to hold those hands ♪

159
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:36,640
♪ But it's just a luxury,
love has turned to nothing ♪
